# Sprint Cycle 12: Production Hardening, Zero-Downtime Session Resilience & Edge Telemetry Stabilization

## Task A: Harden Telemetry & Edge Resilience
- Implemented a circuit breaker in `src/lib/telemetry.js` to silence console spam and fallback to offline queuing in `localStorage` when edge workers timeout or return 5xx errors.
- Refined `TelemetryBar.jsx` for mobile responsiveness (collapsed UI at `< 768px`) and ensured telemetry animations run smoothly without parent tree re-renders.
- Updated `workers/telemetry-worker.js` to properly return wildcard CORS headers on `OPTIONS` checks, and default to `204 No Content` for successful payload processing and graceful queue fallbacks.
- Fixed `workers/telemetry-worker.test.js` to account for wildcard `*` CORS expectations.

## Task B: Auth Streamlining & Silent Token Renewal
- Updated `src/hooks/useAximAuth.js` to maintain a silent background `isReconnecting` state. Sessions are optimistically retained during sporadic timeouts or network disruptions instead of immediately logging the user out.
- Adjusted `ProtectedRoute.jsx` to render a non-intrusive degraded fallback ("Re-establishing Uplink...") when `isReconnecting` is active.
- Modified `src/lib/auth-handoff.js` to extract and append the user's role string to SSO cross-app URLs to maintain roles across domains.

## Task C: UI/UX Micro-Interactions & Responsive Alignment
- Edited `Header.jsx` to correctly apply accessibility standards `aria-current="page"` to active links, preventing layout shifts.
- Fixed `OnyxTerminal.jsx` scrolling behavior to intelligently auto-scroll only if the operator was already pinned to the bottom of the log interface.

## Pre-Commit Verification
- `npm run build` succeeds cleanly.
- `npx vitest run` tests all pass.
- `npx eslint src` verified without warnings.
